    description: "FOUND 2026-09-02 by carrying 0006's own adjudicated labels forward against a\nfresh collect at dev 8f1a240b0e, on the SAME 16-repo cohort. No new\nadjudication was involved: these are situations 0006's panel labelled TP and\nWI-gibom's vacuity pass labelled USEFUL, which the tool NO LONGER REPORTS.\n\n    0006 as published    112 situations   38 headline TP   11 vacuous  27 useful\n    still reported        67              20               0          20\n    NO LONGER reported    45              18              11           7\n\nAll 11 vacuous deductions are gone, which is the intended effect of WI-rigut\n(haskell IORef/STRef) and PR #541 (bash discard-only redirects). But SEVEN of\nthe 27 USEFUL true positives went with them -- 26% of the useful recall on this\ncohort:\n\n  gocryptfs#2          environ -> `>` @ redirect     test.bash\n  guacamole-client#0   environ -> `>` @ redirect     doc/licenses/generate-license-files.sh\n  guacamole-client#6   environ -> `>>` @ redirect    guacamole-docker/entrypoint.d/500-generate-tomcat-catalina-base.sh\n  rabbitmq#0           get_env -> format @ io_lib    deps/rabbit/src/rabbit_logger_exchange_h.erl\n  rabbitmq#4           get_env -> format @ io_lib    deps/rabbit/src/rabbit_vhost.erl\n  rabbitmq#6           get_env -> format @ io_lib    deps/rabbit/src/rabbit_definitions.erl\n  ArkLib#6             argv -> write @ file          scripts/inject_nav.py\n\n*** gocryptfs#2 IS THE ONE TO READ FIRST, AND 0006's OWN RECORD PREDICTS IT. ***\nThat record documents it as a REVERSAL caught only on a second pass:\n\n  \"gocryptfs#2 was first labelled discard-only on the same evidence shape --\n   four `>` sites, all /dev/null. A second pass over the raw file found a\n   FIFTH: L42 `exec 200> \"$LOCKFILE\"`, a numbered-fd redirect to a real path,\n   and the path is env-derived (TMPDIR -> TESTDIR -> LOCKFILE). It is a genuine\n   environment -> host-filesystem write. The first cut would have published\n   23.2%.\"\n\nPRIME SUSPECT: PR #541, which \"refuses the boundary when EVERY collapsed call\nsite discards\". If its per-site test does not see `exec 200>` as a\nnon-discarding site -- the same numbered-fd form the human second pass nearly\nmissed -- then #541 reproduces the error 0006 caught by hand, in code, silently.\nThe two guacamole-client redirects are the same family and the same suspect.\n\nNOT YET DIAGNOSED, and deliberately not asserted: the three rabbitmq\n`get_env -> io_lib:format` losses and ArkLib#6 have no named suspect. They may\nbe catalogue removals, collapse-key changes, or a matching regression.\n\nMETHOD CAVEAT. Situations were matched on\n(repo, claim_id, source_symbol, sink_symbol), because flow_id is\n{repo}:{claim}:{INDEX} and the index shifts whenever a situation is added or\nremoved upstream. A flow whose endpoints are unchanged but whose PATH changed\ncounts as surviving here."  # 6e4a
    fields:  # 6e4a
      statement: "A fix that removes a vacuous finding must not remove an adjudicated USEFUL true positive: 7 of 0006's 27 useful TPs are no longer reported"  # 6e4a
      root_cause: "UNDIAGNOSED for 4 of 7. Prime suspect for the 3 bash redirect losses is PR #541 (refuse the boundary when EVERY collapsed call site discards): gocryptfs#2's genuine site is 'exec 200> $LOCKFILE', a NUMBERED-FD redirect to an env-derived path, which 0006's human second pass nearly missed and which #541's per-site discard test may not recognise as non-discarding. The 3 rabbitmq get_env->io_lib:format losses and ArkLib#6 argv->file.write have no named suspect and were not investigated."  # 6e4a
