    fields:  # 3b68
      root_cause: "RESOLVED, and the filed root_cause was wrong twice. (1) The '7 lost' figure was a matcher artifact: keying on sink_symbol, which names a COLLAPSE REPRESENTATIVE, counted five re-collapsed situations as losses. Source-keyed match gives ONE. (2) PR #541 was named as prime suspect and is cleared by fixture: target_kinds_cross_no_boundary requires ALL kinds non-crossing and 'unresolved' is not in _NON_CROSSING_TARGET_KINDS. The genuine defect was INV-jurif's env-read rule refusing the conditional-default idiom (if [[ -z ${TMPDIR:-} ]]; then TMPDIR=...), fixed in PR #721."  # 3b68
- op: discuss  # 7eef
  at: '2026-09-02T23:28:00Z'  # 7eef
  by: agent  # 7eef
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7eef
  clock: 3  # 7eef
  nonce: 7eef  # 7eef
  message: "CORRECTION TO MY OWN FILING, AND IT IS A LARGE ONE. This item was filed on\n\"7 of 27 useful true positives are no longer reported\". The real figure is ONE,\nand that one looks like a CORRECT refusal. The 7 was an artifact of the matcher\nI used to produce it.\n\nWHAT WENT WRONG. I matched 0006's sampled situations into the new collection on\n(repo, claim_id, source_symbol, sink_symbol). The sink symbol names the\nCOLLAPSED situation's representative primitive, and INV-vukiv's collapse rule\nmeans that representative can change when the member set changes -- so the same\nflow, from the same source, re-collapsing under `>>` instead of `>` reads as a\ndifferent situation and therefore as a loss. Re-run with a source-keyed match\n(repo, claim_id, source_symbol), holding everything else fixed:\n\n    key                          survivors  usefulTP  lostUseful  useful%\n    (repo, claim, src, SINK)          68       21          6       30.9\n    (repo, claim, src)                78       26          1       33.3\n\nFive of the six were never lost. guacamole-client#0 is the clearest: its flow is\nstill reported from the same file, with the sink primitive moved from `>` to\n`>>`.\n\nWHAT WAS REAL, AND IT IS FIXED. One of the seven was a genuine defect and PR\n#721 closes it: INV-jurif's env-read rule (\"a name never ASSIGNED in this file\")\nrefused the conditional-default idiom, `if [[ -z ${TMPDIR:-} ]]; then\nTMPDIR=/var/tmp; fi`. gocryptfs/test.bash is back to `violated` on the\nproduction path -- and that is precisely the flow 0006's panel reached a\ntrue-positive label on only at the SECOND pass, after finding\n`exec 200> \"$LOCKFILE\"`.\n\nTHE ONE REMAINDER, and I am NOT calling it a regression. guacamole-client#6\n(500-generate-tomcat-catalina-base.sh, environ -> `>>`) is genuinely no longer\nreported. Read against source, the redirect target is\n`\"$CATALINA_BASE/conf/catalina.properties\"` and CATALINA_BASE is assigned on\nline 34 from `mktemp -p /tmp -d`. The write target is therefore NOT env-derived,\nand WI-zovuz's origin-names gate refusing it is the gate working. Whether the\n2026-08-25 panel's TP label was right is an ADJUDICATION question and belongs to\nthe re-measurement, not to a defect item.\n\nMY PRIME SUSPECT WAS ALSO WRONG, recorded because it was in this item's\nroot_cause. I named PR #541 (\"refuse the boundary when EVERY collapsed call site\ndiscards\"). It is not implicated: `target_kinds_cross_no_boundary` requires\nALL kinds to be non-crossing, `unresolved` is not in\n`_NON_CROSSING_TARGET_KINDS`, and a fixture with two /dev/null redirects plus\n`exec 200> \"$LOCKFILE\"` emits the third edge with kind=unresolved. Tested rather\nthan reasoned about, which is how the wrong suspect was cleared.\n\nSTATUS: satisfied. The invariant as stated -- a fix that removes a vacuous\nfinding must not remove an adjudicated useful true positive -- holds on the\nmeasured evidence: one such removal, fixed; one refusal that is defensible on\nits own source and is an adjudication question rather than a defect.\n\nMETHOD NOTE WORTH CARRYING: a situation's SINK SYMBOL is not a stable identity\nacross runs, because it names a collapse representative. Any future\ncarry-forward of adjudicated labels should key on the source and the claim, and\nreport the sink separately."  # 7eef
